= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @workers: The blue collar working class, our traditional support base.
- @white_collar_workers: The middle class of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @self_employed: The middle class of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who have felt neglected by us in the past.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @catholics: Catholics, who typically support the Center Party.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 0.5 if unemployed >= 15; workers_spd -= 0.5 if unemployed >= 25; resources -= 1; workers_spd += 1.8*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?]

@white_collar_workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: white_collar_workers_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; white_collar_workers_spd -= 0.5 if unemployed >= 15; white_collar_workers_spd -= 0.5 if unemployed >= 25;

We have increased our campaigning among the employed middle class.

@self_employed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: self_employed_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; self_employed_spd -= 0.5 if nationalism >= 51 or socialism <= 49

We have increased our campaigning among the self employed. [? if nationalism >= 51: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if socialism <= 49: Anti-socialism is widespread among this group. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent); rural_spd -= 0.5 if socialism <= 49; resources -= 1; rural_spd += 1.5*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if rural_policy < 2: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]
